# Who owns each service. GitHub asks a service's owners to review every pull
# request that changes it, and your ruleset can require one of them to approve.
#
# To set it up (Chapter 3.2):
#   1. Replace each <placeholder> with a teammate's GitHub username,
#      including the @, for example @octocat.
#   2. Remove the "# " at the start of each rule below.
#
# List two people per service, an owner and a backup. GitHub never counts an
# approval on your own pull request, so a service with a single owner would
# block that owner's own changes. When several lines match a file, the last
# one wins, and every owner for a path must be on the same line.

# Everything not listed below belongs to the whole team.
# *                        <teammate> <teammate> <teammate>

# /employees-service/      <owner> <backup>
# /projects-service/       <owner> <backup>
# /notifications-service/  <owner> <backup>
# /web/                    <owner> <backup>

# The service you build together belongs to everyone.
# /assignments-service/    <teammate> <teammate> <teammate>
